## Interactive Deploy Menus (this repo)

One review menu: `[o]verwrite` / `[a]ccept & adopt` / `[m]erge & adopt` /
`[s]kip` / `[x]abort`; `[a]` and `[m]` only when the caller passed an adopt
target; JSON gets the same choices per field, without `[m]`. Choices:
`.claude/rules/agentic-standards.md` "Managed-file review choices and merge".

PS1 and bash menus MUST show identical options in identical order. Every return
value from `Deploy-ManagedFile` / `deploy_managed_file` MUST be handled at
**every call site**: `created`, `updated`, `verified`, `accept & adopt`,
`skipped`, `failed` (on `failed` the library restored its backups and recorded
the error once with `write_error` under the tool name the caller passed: WHAT the
failed step, REASON the write, AI merge, adopt filter or validation error; on `skipped` it recorded the warning once; the caller records the outcome
with the deploy tracker, writes no second WARN or ERROR record, and continues;
`reference/logging.md` section 8). Scripts with multiple call sites (e.g., setup-user-claude
deploys both CLAUDE.md and rules) must handle all return values at each site
independently. **Known limitation:** Step 30 validates at file level, not
call-site level -- manual audit required for multi-deployment scripts.
Non-interactive fallback required (`AITOOLS_FORCE`/`--force`, non-terminal stdin -> overwrite, no menu, so no AI merge starts); EOF at a prompt -> that prompt's default + warn (review menu and any JSON field that offers overwrite: overwrite; JSON field only in LOCAL, no overwrite offered: skip; merge preview: reject; refine feedback: empty, one more AI merge attempt); installers apply the same rule to their own prompts.
`[x]abort` logs an error and exits 2; a bare exit 2 is a user abort (D-TS13); it ends this setup script. Exit 2 from `deploy-harness` (installer Step 8b, first script of the `aitools` sync) stops the run: the runner records one warning, `write_warn "harness files" "aborted by user"`, runs no further step, renders the summary and exits 2. Exit 2 from any other setup script is handled like any failure: the runner's relay records one error, WHAT `<label> failed (exit 2)`, REASON `aborted by user`, counted in the runner's error count, and the run continues with the next script (the profile-mirror menu's "stop the run" text included). The script's own abort line is logged and counted, not recorded (`reference/logging.md` 8.3 "A user abort").

PS1 console I/O: `[Console]::ReadLine/WriteLine`. Read external command output
via temp file + `[IO.File]::ReadAllText(..., UTF8)` (not pipeline capture).

Bash: `read -r < /dev/tty` / `printf ... > /dev/tty`.

Full spec: `reference/managed-file-deployment.md`.
